  "content": "Support services for cybercriminals continue to grow as well, with the success of money laundering services that allows funds from financial fraud and cybercrime to be mixed with legitimate funds to make investigations more difficult. The ecosystem surrounding money laundering has evolved in the past few years. North Korea cyber-criminals move larger amounts of money than other threat actors, but rely on Chinese-language networks for transferring funds. Often, North Korean groups hold onto gains for 45 days before laundering funds, but that is more of a pattern, not a rule, Chainalysis' Jardine says.",
